    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1063">

                <pb facs="0978" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/322</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Chargé d’Affaires</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Borghetti</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Italian Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Manchester, Massachusetts</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-13">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 13, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 14</hi>.] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Translation]</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 1267]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: By order of my
                    Government I have the honor to inform your excellency that by Royal decree of
                    the 6th instant the limit of territorial waters at sea, for the purposes of
                    neutrality, has been fixed at six nautical miles, and that special rules will be
                    framed for the determination of the said territorial waters in bays, bights, and
                    gulfs, in accordance with Article 2 of the said decree.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1063-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>This affords me a welcome opportunity to renew [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Borghetti</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1063-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1063-f1-content">
                <p>A similar extension of the limit of territorial waters (to five miles) decreed by
                    the Uruguayan Government on August 7, was transmitted by the Minister in Uruguay
                    in his No. 700, August 13 (File No. 763.72111/438).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
